IMPORT prelude

-- Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998 -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts in days ("within 28 days after the day on which the decision was made", s 45(2);
-- "within 28 days ... after receiving a request", s 46(1); "within 28 days after", s 49(2); "within 30 days after the
-- day on which the application is lodged", s 68(4); "60 days after making the order", s 117(1)(a); "within 14 days",
-- s 117(2); "within 45 days after receiving it", s 117(3); "within 28 days after the day of the order", s 148(2)(a);
-- "no later than 14 days after the day on which leave is granted", s 148(3)(a); "the minimum period ... is 14 days",
-- s 114(2)) and once in months ("more than 12 months before the application was made", Sch 1 cl 18).
--
-- "Within n days after" a day ends at the end of the day n days later (fork F1). A period of months after a day ends on
-- the same day of the month that many months later; where that month has no such day, on its last day (fork F2).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Victorian
-- Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998 (Vic), Act No. 53/1998, Version No. 145 (28 July 2026), not the authorised
